From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: gadget: read a pending RX packet instead of flushing it

When an OUT request is queued on an idle endpoint, musb_ep_restart()
flushed the RX FIFO. A packet that arrived while no request was queued
was thrown away. FunctionFS queues one request per read(), so with MTP
(umtprd) the data phase that follows a command right away was lost and
the host hung waiting (SendObjectInfo / SendObject never completed).

Read the pending packet with rxstate(), as for TX with txstate().

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
index 016d3f3fc..c204c8c4c 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
@@ -1162,18 +1162,16 @@ void musb_free_request(struct usb_ep *ep, struct usb_request *req)
  */
 void musb_ep_restart(struct musb *musb, struct musb_request *req)
 {
-	u16 csr;
-	void __iomem *epio = req->ep->hw_ep->regs;
-
 	trace_musb_req_start(req);
 	musb_ep_select(musb->mregs, req->epnum);
 	if (req->tx) {
 		txstate(musb, req);
 	} else {
-		csr = musb_readw(epio, MUSB_RXCSR);
-		csr |= MUSB_RXCSR_FLUSHFIFO | MUSB_RXCSR_P_WZC_BITS;
-		musb_writew(epio, MUSB_RXCSR, csr);
-		musb_writew(epio, MUSB_RXCSR, csr);
+		/* A packet may already be waiting in the FIFO: it arrived while no
+		 * request was queued (FunctionFS queues one per read()). Read it
+		 * instead of flushing it, or that OUT packet is lost.
+		 */
+		rxstate(musb, req);
 	}
 }
 
